  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Voice of Command (X)" id="d28b-912d-2dce-1b5a" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>At the start of your Shooting phase, a model with this rule may issue up to X orders, each to a different friendly Astra Militarum Infantry unit within 12" (including its own unit). The ordered unit takes a Leadership test using the officer's Leadership; if it passes, the order takes effect until the end of the turn. A unit may receive only one order per turn. Order: Effect. Bring It Down!: The unit may re-roll failed to-wound and armour penetration rolls against Vehicles, Dreadnoughts and Monstrous Creatures.. First Rank, Fire! Second Rank, Fire!: Lasguns and hot-shot lasguns in the unit fire one additional shot. The unit may not move or Advance this turn.. Fix Bayonets!: The unit adds 1 to its Attacks Characteristic in the next Assault phase.. Get Back in the Fight!: The unit is no longer Pinned or Falling Back, and may shoot this phase.. Move! Move! Move!: Instead of shooting, the unit moves up to D6 plus its Initiative Characteristic in inches.. Take Aim!: The unit may re-roll to-hit rolls of 1 when shooting..</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Combined Squad" id="ddde-9e4f-aa9f-8f6f" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>Infantry Squads have the option of forming Combined Squads. The decision to form Combined Squads must be made immediately before determining your Warlord Traits. If the Astra Militarum player wishes to deploy his forces in this way, then any Infantry Squad may join another Infantry Squad from the same platoon. For example, an Infantry Platoon consisting of a Platoon Command Squad and three 10-man Infantry Squads can instead choose to deploy as a Platoon Command Squad and a single 30-man Infantry Squad, or a Platoon Command Squad, a 10-man Infantry Squad and a 20-man Infantry Squad. If you decide to form Combined Squads in this manner, they are treated as a single unit for whole of the game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Heavy Weapons Team" id="ed0c-7c13-1822-4375" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>Infantry heavy weapons are typically crewed by a team of two men; one fires the weapon while the other supplies the ammunition, and between them they can relocate their weapon if needs be. For all game purposes, each Heavy Weapons Team or Veteran Weapons Team is treated as a single model with the Bulky special rule – it may only fire one weapon in the Shooting phase, only gains one additional Attack for charging, and only counts as one model for Morale checks, for example.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Senior Officer" id="5ee9-fae7-8e24-efcb" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>Lord Commissars and Tempestor Primes are Senior Officers. A Senior Officer may take Heirlooms of Conquest (see Wargear); only one of each heirloom may be taken per army.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Abhuman" id="b104-17b7-47de-cfd1" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>Ogryns, Bullgryns and Ratlings may not receive orders unless an order is issued by Nork Deddog or an officer within 6".</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fury of the Regiment" id="928d-06ac-2dfe-9f35" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>Line troopers drill endlessly with the lasgun until a regiment can lay down a curtain of fire that halts any foe. If a model with this rule has not moved or Run during its controlling player's Movement phase, it may add one to the number of shots fired when making a Shooting Attack with a Las weapon (this does not include lascannons or heavy lascannons).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Jungle Ambush" id="0c77-151c-99aa-1d8a" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>On a turn in which this unit charges or is charged, its models add 1 to their To Wound rolls in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Regiment (X)" id="3db4-0599-0496-8aaf" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>See Regiments, below.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Regimental Line (X)" id="2218-83b3-5fc9-210e" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>A unit with this rule is a Support Squad Troops choice. If it is in a detachment whose Regiment (X) matches X, it loses the Support Squad special rule, and all its models gain the Line Sub-type and the Fury of the Regiment special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shock Troops" id="c826-b0d7-018e-7a7d" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>At the end of your turn, if this unit is within 3" of an objective you control, that objective stays under your control even if no models are within range of it, until an enemy unit that can score or deny controls it at the end of any turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealth" id="b4c5-0f37-7c2e-ddd7" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>If the model has not moved this turn, it cannot be targeted by ranged attacks from more than 12" away.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Summary Execution" id="b4e7-27bd-dadf-a361" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>If a unit containing a Commissar fails a Morale check or Pinning test, the Commissar may execute one model of your choice from the unit (not the Commissar or another character). The unit then counts as having passed the test, and uses the Commissar's Leadership for the rest of the turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Leman Russ Commander" id="7232-b367-a008-1989" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>A Tank Commander starts the game in a Leman Russ tank, leading a Leman Russ Squadron. Note that any type of Leman Russ can be taken as the Tank Commander's vehicle, and that it can have any upgrades usually available to that type of tank. The Tank Commander's tank is a character, has Ballistic Skill 4 and can be chosen as your army's Warlord. If his tank is Wrecked or suffers an Explodes! result, the Tank Commander is killed. A Tank Commander and his Leman Russ Squadron count as an HQ choice for the entire of the battle. The Tank Commander's Leman Russ cannot leave the unit or join another unit, even if the rest of his squadron are destroyed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tank Orders (X)" id="e741-185f-25c0-7a03" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>A Tank Commander may issue up to X orders to Astra Militarum vehicles within 12", using the same procedure: **Full Throttle!** (the vehicle may move an extra 6" but may not shoot), **Gunners, Kill on Sight!** (re-roll to-hit rolls of 1), or **Strike and Shroud!** (after shooting, the vehicle counts as obscured until your next turn).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Psykana (X)" id="a3ac-8cfc-7f26-2fa4" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>Every sanctioned psyker knows the Psychic Maelstrom psychic weapon, plus X psychic powers from the table below, chosen when the army is built. Power: Kind, Phase, Effect. Gaze of the Emperor: Psychic weapon, Shooting, Beam: 24", S8, AP 2, Assault 1, Lance, Psychic. Mental Fortitude: Psychic power, Movement (start), One friendly unit within 12" automatically passes Morale checks and Pinning tests until the start of your next turn.. Nightshroud: Psychic power, Movement (start), One friendly unit within 12" gains Shrouded (5+) until the start of your next turn.. Psychic Barrier: Psychic power, Movement (start), One friendly unit within 12" gains a 5+ Invulnerable Save until the start of your next turn.. Psychic Maelstrom: Psychic weapon, Shooting, 18", S5, AP 4, Assault D6, Psychic. Terrifying Visions: Psychic power, Shooting, One enemy unit within 18" subtracts 2 from its Leadership until the start of your next turn..</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="e95f-b73d-1ff4-2879" hidden="false" publicationId="0fda-9dad-a0bf-40e6">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
